# A snapshot pins byte-for-byte tokenization, so a fixture and its snapshot must reach
# every platform with the same line endings. Without this a Windows checkout converts
# them and every snapshot drifts for reasons that have nothing to do with the grammar.
#
# A snapshot that reached a reader with CRLF fails a second way, and silently: the annotation regex
# ends on `$`, and a carriage return counts as a line terminator to both `.` and `$`, so the reader
# answers a file full of annotations as one carrying none. Every gate over the pinned snapshots then
# reports green having measured nothing. `tools/bytes-on-disk.test.js` holds the tree to this line,
# and `readSnapshot` takes a carriage return anyway, for a file that arrives by another road.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.vsix binary

# A corpus specimen carrying control characters on purpose. Nothing normalizes its bytes.
corpus/tid/control-char.tid binary
